ight-winger, but he had a calm&nbsp;&nbsp; voice. Yeah. John McCain. I disagree with John&nbsp; McCain on 95% of the issues, but man, nobody,&nbsp;&nbsp; nobody on Capitol Hill was a bigger supporter of&nbsp; mine than John McCain. That's amazing.RACL wants&nbsp;&nbsp; to know if we have any updates on Jermall&nbsp; Thomas. I'm afraid not. Last I'd heard was,&nbsp;&nbsp; you know, he was recovering. You know, it's a&nbsp; process. Let me see if I have his cell phone.&nbsp;&nbsp; I must. I have it. OK, good. Yeah. If you don't&nbsp; have it, I'll send it to you. All right, John,&nbsp;&nbsp; we have a few minutes left. I have&nbsp; it.So Viktor Orbán, PM of Hungary,&nbsp;&nbsp; vetoed—any European country's leader can veto any&nbsp; EU decision to celebrate the fourth anniversary of&nbsp;&nbsp; the Russian invasion of Ukraine. EU was going to&nbsp; lend a bunch of money more to Ukraine. I you know,&nbsp;&nbsp; it's like not really that generous, but lend it&nbsp; to them and also impose new sanctions against&nbsp;&nbsp; Russia. I don't know what new sanctions they found&nbsp; hiding between the sofa cushions, but... And but&nbsp;&nbsp; Viktor Orbán is pissed because the Ukrainians&nbsp; are accused in his mind of disrupting this&nbsp;&nbsp; oil pipeline from Russia that goes via Ukraine to&nbsp; Hungary and Slovakia and he's like you're cutting&nbsp;&nbsp; off our oil yet another—no more money to the&nbsp; Ukrainians. Yeah, yet another winter right? Yeah,&nbsp;&nbsp; yet another winter.I'm inclined to believe the&nbsp; Ukrainians are guilty of what they're accused of&nbsp;&nbsp; here. What do you think? Yeah, I'm no fan of&nbsp; Orbán, but I think he's right. And you know,&nbsp;&nbsp; and so he's being accused of—I mean, the other&nbsp; thing is, do you really at this point want to&nbsp;&nbsp; throw good money after bad? I mean, that's&nbsp; a good question. I don't like as an American&nbsp;&nbsp; taxpayer. I don't. I mean, whatever you think of&nbsp; the cause, I mean, the Ukrainians are not going to&nbsp;&nbsp; win this. And so also, it was very funny to me,&nbsp; Zelensky recently said, you know, pointed out,&nbsp;&nbsp; well, Russia hasn't achieved all their goals. And&nbsp; then Russia's like, we have not achieved all our&nbsp;&nbsp; goals. That's why it's still going on. It was&nbsp; pretty funny. This is really characteristically&nbsp;&nbsp; Russian response.Yeah, it is. And you know, this&nbsp; is the thing too. It comes back to the question&nbsp;&nbsp; of why won't the Russians settle this? Because&nbsp; they're winning. There's no reason to settle this.&nbsp;&nbsp; They're winning.Hey, this is a good suggestion.&nbsp; Flandrina, have you guys considered setting up a&nbsp;&nbsp; way we can submit questions before the show? Oh,&nbsp; that's a good question. Well, there is a way. Oh,&nbsp;&nbsp; is there? Yeah, I mean, we have an email address.&nbsp; We could just— I didn't even know we had an email&nbsp;&nbsp; address. We do. So let me see if I can. So we&nbsp; could. But let me talk to Robby and find out&nbsp;&nbsp; what the best way to do this is. Maybe because we&nbsp; need a way for them to be handleable and sort of&nbsp;&nbsp; arrangeable in a way for Robby to be able to put&nbsp; them up. Because currently, Robby filters them&nbsp;&nbsp; through and posts them. And then we watch them&nbsp; in real time. But he sorts through so we don't&nbsp;&nbsp; have to read all the non-question comments.&nbsp; So when Robby's not available, like as today,&nbsp;&nbsp; there's no way to do that. But that's a great&nbsp; idea. We could just set up a question inbox. And&nbsp;&nbsp; the thing is I don't want to open zillions of&nbsp; emails. So I'm wondering what the best logistical&nbsp;&nbsp; way to do that is. I don't know. I guess maybe you&nbsp; could just put the question in the subject line,&nbsp;&nbsp; right? Then you could just see it. You see it&nbsp; all as a list. That's probably the way. Or we&nbsp;&nbsp; could set up a WhatsApp or something like that.&nbsp; It's a good idea.We only have about a minute or&nbsp;&nbsp; a minute and a half left. I've got to ask you&nbsp; as a New Yorker, what do we make of this giant&nbsp;&nbsp; snowball fight yesterday? Oh, good. I'm glad&nbsp; you brought that up. So Washington Square Park&nbsp;&nbsp; in Greenwich Village is, you know, basically has&nbsp; always been kind like the center of counterculture&nbsp;&nbsp; fun in New York. It's where the Halloween parade&nbsp; ends up in a big party. It's in the summer, it's&nbsp;&nbsp; kind of raucous. You're always able to buy drugs&nbsp; there. And there's always like street performances&nbsp;&nbsp; and stuff. So anyway, a spontaneous snowball&nbsp; fight broke out between young people, mostly boys,&nbsp;&nbsp; in the park. Someone dropped a dime on the&nbsp; snowball fight and called 911. Because that's what&nbsp;&nbsp; you do when somebody is gonna throw snow. Right,&nbsp; these are obviously...Well, this reminds me of the&nbsp;&nbsp; time in the early 80s when I had first moved to&nbsp; New York and there were police helicopters over&nbsp;&nbsp; my apartment. Literally, there was a raccoon in&nbsp; the street and the NYPD had been dispatched to do&nbsp;&nbsp; something about it. I'm like, there's nothing to&nbsp; do. It is a raccoon. Just ignore it. But anyway,&nbsp;&nbsp; yeah, so they called the cops. The cops came&nbsp; and then the kids started throwing snowballs&nbsp;&nbsp; at the cops.The cops are acting like it was a 9/11&nbsp; terrorist act and the police unions are whinging&nbsp;&nbsp; and they're pressuring the mayor. The mayor had a&nbsp; pretty good response. This is right-wing [ __ ].&nbsp;&nbsp; The cops shouldn't have responded at all. To&nbsp; the extent that I have any sympathy here for&nbsp;&nbsp; the police, it was very wet, icy snow and it was&nbsp; probably not a lot of fun to catch a big, wet,&nbsp;&nbsp; icy snowball in the back of the head. Cops&nbsp; claim to have been mildly injured. So that&nbsp;&nbsp; kind of sucks. The cops shouldn't have been there&nbsp; in the first place, though, is my take. What's&nbsp;&nbsp; yours? Yeah, the cops shouldn't have been there in&nbsp; the first place. But the New York Post should be&nbsp;&nbsp; ashamed of itself for making it this Mum Donnie&nbsp; versus the cops, you know, riot. Ridiculous.&nbsp;&nbsp; That's not what it was. It was a fight. And I like&nbsp; what Mum Donnie said. He said, you know, leave the&nbsp;&nbsp; cops alone. If you want to throw a snowball at&nbsp; someone throw it at me. There you go.All right,&nbsp;&nbsp; anyway. All right. Thanks, John. We will see you&nbsp; back. We're here Monday through Friday, 9 a.m.,&nbsp;&nbsp; which means we'll be back tomorrow, Thursday at&nbsp; 9 a.m. Eastern time. Thanks for watching. Please&nbsp;&nbsp; stay tuned for TMI Show with me and Milochan&nbsp; coming up right now. Bye. Bye, everybody.


